# Documentation

## Documentation in docs/

- Maintain `docs/project.md` for description and `docs/technical_decisions.md` for architectural choices
- Document every non-obvious decision with context, date, and rationale

## README Contents

- README.md should only include a short project description, how to run/build, and how to develop
- Put deeper details in `docs/project.md` and `docs/technical_decisions.md`

## Translations Belong in Their Own Place

- Store translations/i18n in a dedicated folder with namespace keys
- Do not inline user-facing text in code
